abstract = {<div data-language="eng" data-ev-field="abstract">This paper proposes an improved Life-365TM model, which is used to life cycle cost analysis. The main content is as follows: (1) The existing Life- 365TM model was improved based on artificial neural networks, and the predicted results of the improved model were in good agreement with the experimental data. (2) Adding fibres to concrete can improve the durability of the structure, but is unable to reduce the life cycle cost of structure. (3) The use of BFRP reinforcement instead of steel improves initial construction costs and reduces later maintenance costs. When the 100-year design life is reached, the life cycle cost of a BFRP reinforced fibre concrete structure is 40.61% lower than that of a reinforced concrete structure.<br/></div> © 2022 The authors and IOS Press.},
